        "notes": [
          "Pressure and temperature bounds are the authors' stated range for the derived pressure-scale equation, not a rectangular experimental-data envelope or a phase boundary.",
          "The volume-ratio bounds convert the Tables II-III ambient compression range through the measured initial density and the fitted 0 K cold reference volume."
        ]
      },
      "experimental_pressure_range_gpa": [0.0, 345.0],
      "experimental_temperature_range_k": [300.0, 8500.0],
      "pressure_range_status": "reference_parameterization",
      "determination_method": "experimental",
      "record_kind": "published",
      "notes": "This is the complete empirical pressure-scale form in Appendix B, not a standalone 300 K Vinet fit. Equation (3) and the three globally optimized coefficients define a zero-temperature cold Vinet curve; Equation (B2) adds an absolute thermal pressure that is nonzero at 300 K. The stored Tr=300 K is the Taylor expansion and operational increment reference, not the temperature of the cold curve. Tables II-III label compression by the ambient initial V0=1/rho0 from rho0=3.590 g/cm^3, whereas Equation (B2) defines eta with the smaller fitted cold V0K. The five new shock states span 152-265 GPa; four temperatures span 3088-5676 K and three Eulerian sound velocities are reported. The full quasi-Debye equations and inverse-variance objective are reconstructable from Luo et al. (2023) and Xian et al. (2022), and Peritheos implements that mechanism as SoundVelocityDebyeHelmholtz. The source-author numerical rerun is not reconstructable because the Kono velocity-density coefficients, complete upstream row mask, uncertainty propagation across P-V-T observables, and covariance are not published. A bounded 12-residual fit using only Luo Table I primary rows and a declared Li-2006 velocity-ratio proxy is recorded in the refit ledger; it does not replace this published Appendix-B record. No uncertainty confidence level or covariance is reported for the three optimized cold coefficients, and no errors are reported for c0-c5. The APS article record and full paper were checked; no official supplemental file or machine-readable data deposit is linked.",
