      "experimental_pressure_range_gpa": [0.0, 53.0],
      "experimental_temperature_range_k": [300.0, 2474.0],
      "determination_method": "experimental",
      "notes": "Preferred complete P-V-T parameterization from Table 5 and the conclusion: a 300 K third-order Birch-Murnaghan reference isotherm plus quasi-harmonic Mie-Gruneisen-Debye thermal pressure. The implemented theta(V) relation follows exactly from d ln(theta)/d ln(V)=-gamma with gamma=gamma0(V/V0)^q, i.e. the integrated-Gruneisen law. Table 3's Murnaghan, Vinet, logarithmic, and alternate constrained BM3 fits are preserved separately as nonpreferred room-temperature model-sensitivity records; they are not thermal parameterizations. The static coefficients were obtained from a staged combined-data analysis that included earlier published room-temperature measurements; the bundled Table 2 contains all 61 new observations from this study. The K0' uncertainty is internally inconsistent: formal +/-0.06 in the text (0.05 after Table 3 rounding), pressure-propagated +/-0.2 in the text and abstract, and unexplained +/-0.3 in the conclusion; the stored +/-0.2 follows the explicit error analysis. No official supplement or machine-readable data deposit accompanies the article.",
